# Embeddable — what `comptime` is allowed to return.

use std::nat::{ Nat }

# Structural derivation: see `canDeriveAbilityStructurally`. No ops: it is a compile-time permission.
# Newtypes must opt in (like `Eq`) so a `comptime` cannot silently bake e.g. a `Password`'s hidden
# representation into the artifact; uniformly, no impl means not embeddable (functions, cells, Promise).
## A value `comptime` may return: one fully described by its data, so it survives into the artifact.
## Primitives, records, variants and immutable containers derive; a newtype needs an explicit impl.
## Functions, mutable cells and live handles (`Promise`, `FileHandle`, `Foreign`) never qualify.
ability Embeddable for 'a where { }

## `Nat` is a newtype over a plain `Int`, so stdlib opts it in here.
impl Embeddable for Nat where { }
